   "evidence": "The probe used HEAD's actual SQLite Store and WorkerStore, preserving the database across a simulated coordinator rollback, then submitting a clean heartbeat, successful setup and setup fallback. HEAD copies `previous.updateWarning` when the new heartbeat omits it and the worker release is unchanged, and writes that warning into `setup_warning`. Its completion query additionally requires `json_extract(capabilities,'$.updateWarning') IS NULL`. Base stored current heartbeat capabilities directly and had no such completion guard. Availability does not consult the warning, so the demonstrated consequence is diagnostic."
